Maintainer: Bahadır Yüzbaşı <b.yzb@hotmail.com>
Description: Implements local regression on the two-dimensional Lorentz
    hyperboloid, with ordinary real-valued responses and predictors and
    representation-based kernel weights. Lorentz Hyperbolic Weighted
    Regression (LHWR) is the unpenalized regression foundation; Lorentz
    Hyperbolic Weighted Penalized Regression (LHWPR) extends it with ridge,
    lasso, elastic net, MCP, and SCAD paths. Gaussian and binomial response
    families are supported. Tools include feature and network representation
    constructors, stable hyperbolic and tangent-space distances, bandwidth
    selection, joint bandwidth-regularization tuning, convergence diagnostics,
    coefficient and selection maps, and simulation helpers. Representations
    need not be geographic. Penalized selection summaries are distinct from
    post-selection statistical inference.
